<LegalLayout 
  title="Editorial Policy & Standards" 
  description="Editorial policy, source selection standards, corrections policy, and commercial independence standards for Bangladesh Travel Guide."
  lastUpdated="October 18, 2026"
>
  <p>
    Bangladesh Travel Guide is committed to publishing accurate, factual, and practical travel guidance for foreign tourists visiting Bangladesh. Our mission is to provide clear, actionable information without sensationalism or commercial bias.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Sourcing & Verification Standards</h2>
  <p>
    We prioritize verified, official sources for all factual claims related to travel logistics. Our primary reference points include:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>The Bangladesh Department of Immigration and Passports</li>
    <li>The Civil Aviation Authority of Bangladesh (CAAB)</li>
    <li>Official diplomatic missions and foreign ministry travel advisories</li>
    <li>Public health authorities including the World Health Organization (WHO)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Where practical advice relies on common travel practices rather than official regulation, we explicitly distinguish editorial suggestions from mandatory legal rules.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Commercial Independence</h2>
  <p>
    Our editorial decisions are made independently of our commercial partnerships. Advertisers, affiliate networks, or direct sponsors do not have influence over our guide ratings, factual reporting, safety advisories, or destination coverage.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Corrections Policy</h2>
  <p>
    Immigration rules, entry fees, and travel requirements change frequently. When an error, outdated policy, or factual inaccuracy is identified, we promptly review and update the affected article with a visible "Last Verified" date. If you notice a requirement that has changed, please inform us via our <a href="/contact/">Contact Page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>